{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function createHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/createHotkeySequence.svelte.ts#L72","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/createHotkeySequence.svelte.ts:72"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register a global keyboard shortcut sequence for the current component."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Shift+R"},{"type":"text","value":" then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Shift+T"},{"type":"text","value":"). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sequence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sequence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MaybeGetter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequence"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"callback","children":[{"type":"text","value":"callback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyCallback"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MaybeGetter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/CreateHotkeySequenceOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CreateHotkeySequenceOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"> = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createHotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  // Scroll to top when 'G G' is pressed\n  createHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => {\n    scrollToTop()\n  })\n\n  // Delete line when 'D D' is pressed\n  createHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => {\n    deleteLine()\n  })\n\n  // Delete inner word when 'D I W' is pressed\n  createHotkeySequence(['D', 'I', 'W'], () => {\n    deleteInnerWord()\n  }, { timeout: 500 })\n\n  // Same modifier on consecutive steps (bare Shift between chords is ignored)\n  createHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => {\n    nextAction()\n  })\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  ....\n</div>","lang":"svelte"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"sequence","text":"sequence","level":3},{"id":"callback","text":"callback","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/createHotkeySequence.svelte.ts:72](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/createHotkeySequence.svelte.ts#L72)\n\nRegister a global keyboard shortcut sequence for the current component.\n\nEach step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. `Shift+R` then `Shift+T`). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### sequence\n\n`MaybeGetter`\\<`HotkeySequence`\\>\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\n### options?\n\n`MaybeGetter`\\<[`CreateHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/CreateHotkeySequenceOptions.md)\\> = `{}`\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createHotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  // Scroll to top when 'G G' is pressed\n  createHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => {\n    scrollToTop()\n  })\n\n  // Delete line when 'D D' is pressed\n  createHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => {\n    deleteLine()\n  })\n\n  // Delete inner word when 'D I W' is pressed\n  createHotkeySequence(['D', 'I', 'W'], () => {\n    deleteInnerWord()\n  }, { timeout: 500 })\n\n  // Same modifier on consecutive steps (bare Shift between chords is ignored)\n  createHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => {\n    nextAction()\n  })\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  ....\n</div>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createHotkeySequence\ntitle: createHotkeySequence\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/createHotkeySequence.svelte.ts:72](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/createHotkeySequence.svelte.ts#L72)\n\nRegister a global keyboard shortcut sequence for the current component.\n\nEach step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. `Shift+R` then `Shift+T`). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### sequence\n\n`MaybeGetter`\\<`HotkeySequence`\\>\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\n### options?\n\n`MaybeGetter`\\<[`CreateHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/CreateHotkeySequenceOptions.md)\\> = `{}`\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createHotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  // Scroll to top when 'G G' is pressed\n  createHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => {\n    scrollToTop()\n  })\n\n  // Delete line when 'D D' is pressed\n  createHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => {\n    deleteLine()\n  })\n\n  // Delete inner word when 'D I W' is pressed\n  createHotkeySequence(['D', 'I', 'W'], () => {\n    deleteInnerWord()\n  }, { timeout: 500 })\n\n  // Same modifier on consecutive steps (bare Shift between chords is ignored)\n  createHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => {\n    nextAction()\n  })\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  ....\n</div>\n```\n"}
